2. AN EXAMPLE STUDENT, BEFORE AND AFTER (invented answers)
   Before: crams, reworking the homework and making mnemonics the night before.
    1. F  I always preview the material before I go to class.   <- study cycle: preview
    2. F  I go over my lecture notes as soon as possible after lecture.   <- study cycle: review
    3. F  I do homework without example problems or copying from notes or book.   <- metacognition: answer without looking
    4. F  I regularly go to office hours or tutoring about the homework.
    5. T  I rework all of the homework problems before the test or quiz.
    6. F  I study for this class at least five days per week, outside class.   <- spaced retrieval: spread out
    7. T  I make mnemonics to help me remember facts and equations.
    8. F  I make diagrams or mental pictures of the concepts from class.
    9. F  I am in a study group where we do homework and quiz ourselves.
   10. F  I rework every missed quiz and test item before the next class.   <- metacognition: analyse the gap
   11. F  I can still do well even if I have done poorly so far.   <- attribute results to behavior
   2 true: predicted grade D

   After: the study cycle and self-testing (the arrows above).
    1. T  I always preview the material before I go to class.
    2. T  I go over my lecture notes as soon as possible after lecture.
    3. T  I do homework without example problems or copying from notes or book.
    4. F  I regularly go to office hours or tutoring about the homework.
    5. T  I rework all of the homework problems before the test or quiz.
    6. T  I study for this class at least five days per week, outside class.
    7. T  I make mnemonics to help me remember facts and equations.
    8. F  I make diagrams or mental pictures of the concepts from class.
    9. F  I am in a study group where we do homework and quiz ourselves.
   10. T  I rework every missed quiz and test item before the next class.
   11. T  I can still do well even if I have done poorly so far.
   8 true: predicted grade B

   Same student, 6 behaviors changed, D -> B.
   Nothing on the list asks how clever you are.
